  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively point toward thermally activated, non-uniform diffusion in HEAs and question universal sluggish-diffusion behavior. In particular, R6 reports differential elemental diffusion, surface enrichment/depletion, and a role for vapor pressure during in situ heating, while R13 links grain-boundary density to enhanced outward elemental flux. R11 also shows preferential compositional loss during intense thermal processing, and R4, R16, and R19 support active diffusion at elevated temperature. However, none describes vacuum heating of sub-10-nm AuCoCuNiPt particles, Au/Cu segregation specifically driven by surface-energy minimization, or reshaping-enhanced diffusion followed by Au/Cu evaporation. Thus the literature points in the right direction, but reconstructing the specific nanoparticle intervention and coupled surface-segregation/shape-evolution mechanism would require a substantial new idea."
